WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.740
A garden fountain.

2
00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:04.770
The nozzle sits half a
metre above the water.

3
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.770
The jet follows a parabola: h equals
minus nought point five x squared,

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.730
plus two x, plus nought point five.

5
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.490
It peaks two metres out,
two point five metres high.

6
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.920
Then it falls.

7
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.590
How wide must the bowl be to catch it?

8
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.190
Twice the peak distance?

9
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.810
Right under the peak?

10
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:28.180
In this mission, you'll see a parabola's
axis of symmetry through its vertex,

11
00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:33.870
and use vertex form: a times x
minus h, all squared, plus k.

12
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.730
The jet hits the water when h equals zero,

13
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.510
a zero of the function.

14
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.290
You'll find zeros with
the quadratic formula.

15
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: find how
far out the jet lands.
